      <body>
         <head>Dolly and Molly and the Farmer Man</head>
         <author>Elizabeth Gordon</author>
         <p rend="color(#000000)">{{GUTENBERG_LICENSE}}</p>
         <p rend="start color(#000000)">en-gutenberg-odts/g/GordonElizabeth-DollyAndMollyAndTheFarmerMan_2016.odt</p>
         <p>Transcriber’s Note:</p>
         <p>Some line breaks adjusted to keep consistent 4-line stanzas.</p>
         <p>Variations on Rand McNally name kept as printed.</p>
         <head>DOLLY AND MOLLY<lb/> <lb/>AND<lb/> <lb/>THE FARMER MAN</head>
         <p>
            <hi rend="italic">By</hi>
         </p>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>Dolly and Molly and the Farmer Man</head>
            <p rend="justify">ELIZABETH GORDON</p>
            <p rend="justify">AUTHOR OF THE “DOLLY AND MOLLY SERIES,” “THE</p>
            <p rend="justify">BUTTERFLY BABIES’ BOOK,” “WATERMELON PETE”</p>
            <p rend="justify">“GRANDDAD COCO NUT’S PARTY”</p>
            <p rend="justify">title page: girls at picnic</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Pictures by</hi>
            </p>
            <p rend="justify">FRANCES BEEM</p>
            <p rend="justify">RAND McNALLY &amp; COMPANY</p>
            <p rend="justify">CHICAGO NEW YORK</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Copyright, 1914,</hi>
            </p>
            <p rend="justify">By Rand, McNally &amp; Co.</p>
            <p rend="justify">copyright page: girls dancing</p>
            <p rend="justify">The Rand-McNally Press</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Chicago</hi>
            </p>
            <p rend="justify">grasshopper</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls carrying basket in field</p>
            <p rend="justify">DOLLY AND MOLLY</p>
            <p rend="justify">AND</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE FARMER MAN</p>
            <p rend="justify">Went Dolly and Molly,</p>
            <p rend="justify">one fine summer day,</p>
            <p rend="justify">To watch while the farmer</p>
            <p rend="justify">man made the new hay.</p>
            <p rend="justify">dancing girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls carrying basket outside house</p>
            <p rend="justify">And a beautiful basket of</p>
            <p rend="justify">luncheon they took,</p>
            <p rend="justify">All wrapped in white napkins</p>
            <p rend="justify">by Mary the cook.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls having picnic</p>
            <p rend="justify">He whetted his scythe.</p>
            <p rend="justify">Oh, the big noise it made!</p>
            <p rend="justify">And he cut down that hay,</p>
            <p rend="justify">each spear and each blade.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls carrying basket</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls watching farmer with scythe</p>
            <p rend="justify">  grasshoppers watching hay being cut</p>
            <p rend="justify">The Grasshoppers hoppered,</p>
            <p rend="justify">and gazed in surprise.</p>
            <p rend="justify">You ought to have seen how</p>
            <p rend="justify">they stuck out their eyes!</p>
            <p rend="justify">dancing girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">He took a big fork and he</p>
            <p rend="justify">spread, all around,</p>
            <p rend="justify">That sweet-smelling hay on</p>
            <p rend="justify">the sunshiny ground.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls having picnic</p>
            <p rend="justify">  farmer spreading hay</p>
            <p rend="justify">  toads watching, suitcase in hand</p>
            <p rend="justify">And the Hoppy Toads</p>
            <p rend="justify">blinked sadly, saying, “Oh, well,</p>
            <p rend="justify">We shall just have to move</p>
            <p rend="justify">to the Burdock Hotel.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls carrying basket</p>
            <p rend="justify">Then he raked it in long</p>
            <p rend="justify">rows, and left it to dry,</p>
            <p rend="justify">While they all ate their lunch</p>
            <p rend="justify">’neath a big tree near by.</p>
            <p rend="justify">dancing girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls watching farmer rake hay</p>
            <p rend="justify">And the Robin came too,</p>
            <p rend="justify">saying, “Please give me some,”</p>
            <p rend="justify">So Dolly and Molly each</p>
            <p rend="justify">gave him a crumb.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls having picnic</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls feeding bird</p>
            <p rend="justify">Then the man tossed the hay</p>
            <p rend="justify">in a great shiny heap,</p>
            <p rend="justify">And put on its night cap,</p>
            <p rend="justify">and left it to sleep.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls carrying basket</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls helping put cover over hay</p>
            <p rend="justify">  farmer walking away down path</p>
            <p rend="justify">Then a black and gold Bumblebee</p>
            <p rend="justify">bumbled along,</p>
            <p rend="justify">Saying, “It’s-time-little-girlies-</p>
            <p rend="justify">were-home-where-they-b’long.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">dancing girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls following bumblebee</p>
            <p rend="justify">So Dolly and Molly, all tired</p>
            <p rend="justify">with play,</p>
            <p rend="justify">Just followed the Bumblebee</p>
            <p rend="justify">home all the way.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls having picnic</p>
            <p rend="justify">  grandmother feeding girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">And Grandmother gave them</p>
            <p rend="justify">some milk and some bread,</p>
            <p rend="justify">And lovingly kissed them</p>
            <p rend="justify">and put them to bed.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls carrying basket</p>
            <p rend="justify">And the sleep fairies came</p>
            <p rend="justify">to that little white room,</p>
            <p rend="justify">And sprinkled them over</p>
            <p rend="justify">with sleep flower bloom.</p>
            <p rend="justify">dancing girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">  sleep fairies sprinkling sleep flowers on girls</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls sleeping</p>
            <p rend="justify">And that was the end of</p>
            <p rend="justify">that beautiful day,</p>
            <p rend="justify">When the twins watched</p>
            <p rend="justify">the farmer man make the new hay.</p>
            <p rend="justify">girls having picnic</p>
            <p rend="justify">  girls tending plants</p>
         </div>
